China's League of Legends league is  canceled until further notice all  because of a deadly virus that's been  making headlines this is a very serious  very crazy story so let's just get right  into it all right so first the eSports  part of this news week two of the LPL  has been indefinitely delayed because of  the corona virus which is a deadly virus  that's been ravaging parts of China and  we'll get to more about that in a moment  the LPL was already on break for a Lunar  New Year but when news of the virus  began to spread and the virus itself  began to spread the LPL chose to delay  week two of games indefinitely in order  to better protect the health and safety  of their fans and players notably the  LDL which is China's version of the  Academy League is also delayed  indefinitely as for when things will be  back well we reached out to Riot Games  and got this comment our team in China  is working closely with authorities  there and will continue to monitor the  situation on a daily basis there are a  few more eSports events that have been  or could be impacted by the Chinese  government's reaction to the corona  virus outbreak first will be w es g's  csgo a packed finals in Macau which was  canceled last Wednesday the event was  supposed to run from February 16th to  18th and W ESG has yet to announce if  they'll be holding a replacement event  elsewhere there are also three overwatch  league teams based in China the Chengdu  hunters the Shanghai dragons and the  Hangzhou spark who are all scheduled to  host games in China this year some home  stands are even coming up as soon as  February none of the teams nor Blizzard  has made any statements about whether  they'll be delaying those home stands or  canceling them entirely or continuing as  planned so what is the corona virus well  the virus we're hearing about right now  is actually a specific strain of corona  virus one that we've never encountered  before many fear the situation is  already far worse than government  officials are telling them in Hong Kong  for instance where they still remember  the huge toll from the SARS virus if  you've ever heard of SARS that was  actually another novel strain of corona  virus that we had never encountered  before when it broke out in the early  2000s and if you haven't heard of it or  are too young to remember the outbreak  it was a disease that spread out of Asia  in the early 2000s  killed about 774 people mostly in China  and Hong Kong SARS is another thing that  I'll get back to a little bit later in  this video anyway most coronaviruses  began in animals and this particular  strain is believed to have originated at  a seafood market mu Han which is the  sixth largest city in China this  specific food market was closed on  January 1st after the first symptoms  were discovered on December 8th  however some reports from Chinese  researchers have found that 13 of the 41  first cases of this strain of crota  virus may not have originated in the  market so it's still relatively unclear  where this virus originated anyway the  World Health Organization received its  first reports from Chinese officials on  December 31st when they reported that  there was an outbreak in muha a few  weeks later there were 600 confirmed  cases in China and 18 deaths on January  23rd the Chinese government expanded the  quarantine from Wuhan to Guan gong and  Asia these three cities account for  nearly 20 million people that's more  than the entire population of the  Netherlands if you want a little bit of  perspective what you're seeing here is  really being replicated all over the  country people are worried about leaving  their homes and they're concerned so the  government has been taking a many more  aggressive measures to try to contain  what they've described as the  strengthening of virus within the  quarantine zone people are not allowed  to take any public transit a lot of the  city is on lockdown supermarkets have  been pretty much cleaned out of all  their food and people have been urged to  stay indoors and avoid public places as  of recording there have been nearly  3,000 confirmed cases and at least 80  deaths as a result of the virus that's  now being referred to as 2019 and CoV  those numbers are according to the New  York Times we've also learned that the  virus can now transfer from person to  person not just animal to person which  is what's led to stuff like the  quarantines and of course the LPL  delaying games given that all their  games happen in public places we already  mentioned the quarantine in Wuhan a city  that's larger than New York but the  Chinese government has also canceled  inter province and bus services they've  suspended tours within China and the  Hong Kong government has declared a  state of emergency and closed schools  for at least three weeks things are  getting very serious the US government  has also begun screening people coming  in from Wuhan  to the states and the government is also  on getting American out of LA starting  tonight we're going to begin screening  passengers arriving from Wuhan  into the United States at the three  airports that see the majority of those  passengers the airports are JFK San  Francisco and Los Angeles and one of the  english-language casters for the LPL  munch tweeted out that he and the  majority of the English language  LPL caster desk are leaving China when  we go back to our own country where you  go and you go back to I've been in the  UK UK Australia the Irish safety worried  about the reaction to this strain of the  coronavirus is relatively similar to  SARS which as I mentioned was a strain  of the corona virus that spread across  Asia and around the world in the early  2000s now researchers eventually found  that SARS originated in back from the  Yunnan Province of China but at the end  of the day it was a relatively rare  disease and was declared contained in  2003 pretty shortly after the outbreak  was first reported one of the major  outbreak locations for SARS outside of  China was Toronto which is where I'm  from and I remember that people were  extremely concerned during the outbreak  now we're in a similar situation with a  lot of panic around the globe and people  working to help people which has led to  things like the LTL getting caught up in  the situation notably former pro player  and EDG coach clearlove is from Wuhan  and it appears according to the  translations at least that he's  streaming from there right now on top of  that the inter province bus network is  down right now due to the quarantines so  it may be difficult for LPL players to  get back to their team's headquarters  when the LPL starts back up again it's  all very new says the deputy director of  China's National Health Commission Lieb  in our knowledge is limited and the  epidemic is not in control  we haven't actually been able to confirm  if there are any other players in the  LPL who are in the quarantine zone or  are otherwise affected so we're just  hoping that everyone is  thanks for watching if you want more  content like this hit the sub button and  ring that notification bell for unique  bite-sized videos you won't find  anywhere else hit up our Instagram  Twitter and Facebook pages  [Music]

